{title: 430 - Joy By and By}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]O there'll be joy when the [F]work is done,
[F]Joy when the reapers [Bb]gather home,
[Bb]Bringing the sheaves at [Eb]set of sun
To the [Bb]New Je[G]ru[C7]sa[F]lem.
[Bb]Joy, joy, joy, there'll be [F]joy by and by,
[F7]Joy, joy, joy, where the [Bb]joys [F]never [Bb]die;
[Bb]Joy, [D]joy, [Gm]joy, [Bb7]for the [Eb]day draweth nigh
When the [Bb]workers [F7]gather [Bb]home.

Refrain:
[Bb]Joy, joy, joy, there'll [F]be joy by and by,
[F]Joy, joy, joy, where [Bb]the joys never die;
[Bb]Joy, joy, joy, for [Eb]the day draweth nigh
[Bb]When [G]the [C7]workers [F]gather home.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Sweet are the songs [F]that we hope to sing,
[F]Grateful the thanks [Bb]our hearts shall bring,
[Bb]Praising forever [Eb]Christ our King
[Bb]In [G]the [C7]New [F]Jerusalem.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Pure are the joys [F]that await us there,
[F]Many the [Bb]golden mansions fair;
[Bb]Jesus Himself [Eb]doth them prepare,
[Bb]In [G]the [C7]New [F]Jerusalem.
